# Hermes Agent — env-loader override workaround (local, reversible)

**Applied:** 2026-06-28
**Scope:** This personal MacBook only (`~/.hermes/`)
**Reason:** Hermes' `hermes_cli/env_loader.py:168` calls `_load_dotenv_with_fallback(user_env, override=True)`, which clobbers `os.environ` values with the literal contents of `~/.hermes/.env` on every chat-subprocess spawn. With `op run --env-file=~/.hermes/.env`, this means the secret values resolved from `op://` refs get clobbered back to the literal `op://...` strings, breaking every cloud-routed call.

**Upstream tracking:**
- [NousResearch/hermes-agent#19201](https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/19201) — the bug (12-factor precedence violation; `type/bug`, P2)
- [NousResearch/hermes-agent#18734](https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/pull/18734) — the PR with the `override=True` → `override=False` fix in flight (community-authored, well-reviewed, awaiting merge)
- [NousResearch/hermes-agent#36949](https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/36949) — related feature request: native 1Password (`op://`) secret-source backend
- [LAF-US/IDAHO-VAULT#690](https://github.com/LAF-US/IDAHO-VAULT/issues/690) — our tracker
- [`IDAHO-VAULT/!/SIGNALS/TOUCHING-ME-TOUCHING-NOUS-2026-06-25.md`](https://github.com/LAF-US/IDAHO-VAULT/blob/logan/obsidian/!/SIGNALS/TOUCHING-ME-TOUCHING-NOUS-2026-06-25.md) — witness leaf for the upstream contact arc

