## How to revert (when #18734 lands)

When `hermes update` brings down the upstream fix (`override=False` becomes the default, or `HERMES_DOTENV_OVERRIDE=1` gates the old behavior), pick one:

### Option A — keep the workaround running

It still works regardless of the override flag. Cost: ~17 sequential `op read` calls at every daemon launch, ~5–15 seconds of startup overhead. If that doesn't bother you, no action needed.

### Option B — revert to the simpler `op run` shim

1. **Move op-refs back into `.env`:**
   ```sh
   # Strip the header comment block from .env.op, then append the rest to .env
   grep -v '^#' ~/.hermes/.env.op | grep -v '^$' >> ~/.hermes/.env
   ```
2. **Delete the .env.op file:**
   ```sh
   rm ~/.hermes/.env.op
   ```
3. **Restore the pre-workaround shim from the timestamped backup:**
   ```sh
   ls -t ~/.hermes/bin/hermes-gateway-launch.sh.bak.preworkaround.* | head -1 | xargs -I{} cp {} ~/.hermes/bin/hermes-gateway-launch.sh
   chmod 700 ~/.hermes/bin/hermes-gateway-launch.sh
   ```
4. **Bounce the daemon:**
   ```sh
   launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ai.hermes.gateway.plist
   launchctl load -w ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ai.hermes.gateway.plist
   ```
5. **Verify cloud routes** (Discord login, OpenRouter calls, etc. should succeed).
6. **Optionally delete this README:** `rm ~/.hermes/README-workaround.md`

